conclusion
  Removing one or two roots leaves a cell of circumradius exactly
  2 whose only points of that norm are twice the removed roots, so
  a contact configuration meeting a D_4 root system in 22 or more
  directions lies inside it.
  Removing three leaves the same picture except at the 96 triples
  that are pairwise at 60 degrees, where the circumradius is
  sqrt6 and a region of further directions opens; root_meet.py
  shows that no two directions of that region are 60 degrees
  apart unless both are removed roots.
